# Fixed-date celebrations that are not saints: feasts of the Lord, dedications of churches, All Souls.
# (date, calendar title, display name, life/description, prayer)
CELEBRATIONS = [
('01-03', 'The Most Holy Name of Jesus', 'The Most Holy Name of Jesus',
 'The name Jesus means "God saves". The angel gave it to Mary and Joseph before his birth, and at his name, Saint Paul writes, "every knee should bow, in heaven and on earth".\n\nThe Church honours the holy name by which we are saved, and invites us to call on it with love and reverence.',
 'Lord Jesus Christ, at your holy name every knee shall bow. May your name be always on our lips and in our hearts, so that we may live for you and rest in you for ever. Amen.'),
('02-02', 'Presentation of the Lord', 'The Presentation of the Lord',
 'Forty days after Christmas, Mary and Joseph brought the infant Jesus to the Temple in Jerusalem to present him to the Lord. The aged Simeon took him in his arms and blessed God: "My eyes have seen your salvation, a light for revelation to the Gentiles." The prophetess Anna also spoke of him to all who awaited redemption.\n\nCandles are blessed on this day, which is also the World Day for Consecrated Life.',
 'Lord God, as your Son was presented in the Temple, grant that we too may be presented to you with clean hearts. May Christ, the Light of the nations, shine in our lives. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('03-25', 'Annunciation of the Lord', 'The Annunciation of the Lord',
 'The angel Gabriel was sent to Mary in Nazareth to announce that she would conceive and bear a son, the Son of the Most High. Mary answered: "Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it done to me according to your word." At that moment the Word became flesh.\n\nNine months before Christmas, the Church celebrates the beginning of our salvation.',
 'Lord God, by the angel\'s message your Word took flesh in the womb of the Virgin Mary. As we believe that he is truly God and truly man, may we, like Mary, say "yes" to your will. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('08-05', 'Dedication of the Basilica of Saint Mary Major', 'The Dedication of the Basilica of Saint Mary Major',
 'After the Council of Ephesus proclaimed Mary the Mother of God in 431, Pope Sixtus III built this great basilica in Rome in her honour. It is the oldest church in the West dedicated to Our Lady.\n\nA tradition tells of snow falling on this hill in the heat of August to show where the church should be built.',
 'Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us. Lord God, through the prayers of the Virgin Mary, help us to grow in faith and love, and bring us safely to the glory of heaven. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('08-06', 'Transfiguration of the Lord', 'The Transfiguration of the Lord',
 'Jesus took Peter, James and John up a high mountain, and there he was transfigured before them: his face shone like the sun and his clothes became white as light. Moses and Elijah appeared with him, and a voice from the cloud said: "This is my beloved Son; listen to him."\n\nThe Transfiguration gave the disciples a glimpse of glory to strengthen them before the Cross.',
 'Lord God, in the glorious Transfiguration of your Son you showed us his glory. Help us to listen to him, so that we may share his glory in heaven. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('09-14', 'Exaltation of the Holy Cross', 'The Exaltation of the Holy Cross',
 'The Church lifts up the Cross of Christ, the tree of life on which he died for our salvation. The feast recalls the finding of the True Cross in Jerusalem by Saint Helena and the dedication of the Basilica of the Holy Sepulchre in 335.\n\n"We adore you, O Christ, and we bless you, because by your holy Cross you have redeemed the world."',
 'We adore you, O Christ, and we bless you, because by your holy Cross you have redeemed the world. Lord, may we who have known the mystery of the Cross on earth enjoy its fruits in heaven. Amen.'),
('11-02', 'All Souls', 'The Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed (All Souls)',
 'The day after All Saints, the Church prays for all the faithful departed who are being purified before entering the joy of heaven. Praying for the dead is an ancient Christian practice of love.\n\nPriests may celebrate three Masses today, and many families visit graves and offer Masses for their loved ones.',
 'Eternal rest grant unto them, O Lord, and let perpetual light shine upon them. May they rest in peace. May their souls and the souls of all the faithful departed, through the mercy of God, rest in peace. Amen.'),
('11-09', 'Dedication of the Lateran basilica', 'The Dedication of the Lateran Basilica',
 'The Basilica of Saint John Lateran is the cathedral of Rome, the Pope\'s own cathedral, and is called "the mother and head of all the churches of the city and of the world". It was dedicated around 324, soon after the Church gained freedom.\n\nThe feast celebrates our unity with the Pope, and reminds us that we ourselves are God\'s temple, built of living stones.',
 'Lord God, from living and chosen stones you build an eternal dwelling for your glory. Increase in your Church the spirit of grace, so that your faithful people may grow into the heavenly Jerusalem. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('11-18', 'Dedication of the basilicas of Saints Peter and Paul, Apostles', 'The Dedication of the Basilicas of Saints Peter and Paul',
 'Today the Church remembers the dedication of the two great basilicas of Rome built over the tombs of the Apostles: Saint Peter\'s on the Vatican Hill and Saint Paul\'s Outside the Walls on the road to Ostia. Both were first built in the time of Emperor Constantine in the fourth century.\n\nThe feast honours the two Apostles whose preaching and martyrdom founded the Church of Rome, and invites us to stand firm in the faith they handed on.',
 'Saints Peter and Paul, pray for us. Lord God, defend your Church through the protection of the holy Apostles, so that, as she received the faith through them, she may grow in grace until the end of time. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
('12-25', 'Nativity of the Lord', 'The Nativity of the Lord (Christmas)',
 'Today the Word became flesh and dwelt among us. In Bethlehem the Son of God was born of the Virgin Mary and laid in a manger, and the angels sang: "Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace to people of good will."\n\nChristmas celebrates God\'s love made visible: Emmanuel, God with us.',
 'Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace to people of good will. Lord God, as we rejoice in the birth of your Son, may we who welcome him as Redeemer share in his divine life. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.'),
]
